// @contract: C-219
// A DIVERGING call in a branch arm runs on both targets, and its exit code is
// the process's.
//
// `process.exit(code)` is the stdlib's only `-> Never`. The arm-tail dispatch
// in `lower_branch_arm` executed a `Call` only when its type was `Ty::Unit`, so
// a `Never` call fell through to the deferred-value path — which records the
// call as a capability marker and EMITS NOTHING. The arm lowered to zero ops
// and reported success, so this program built clean and exited 0 on wasm while
// native exited 3 (#1124).
//
// That is the silent-wrong class, reached through a type the match forgot to
// name rather than through an unsupported shape: no wall, no diagnostic, just a
// different answer. The condition here is RUNTIME-valued on purpose — a
// constant condition is folded earlier (#1117) and takes a different path.
import process

effect fn main() -> Unit = {
  println("before-guard")
  let n = list.len(process.args())
  guard n > 99 else process.exit(3)
  println("unreachable")
}
